From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add the USB0 OTG controller

The A733 has a MUSB OTG controller on USB0, next to the EHCI and OHCI
of that port. It shares PHY 0 and the root port with them, and the PHY
driver routes PHY 0 to one of the two by the mode of the port.

Add the controller disabled, with the bus gate and reset of the clock
controller, the device interrupt, and PHY 0 as PHY and extcon. Boards
enable it and set dr_mode.

Not covered: the shared USB bus gate, which stays with the EHCI and
OHCI nodes, as the binding has one clock.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted; the USB0 controller binds and, as a
gadget on J16, enumerates at high speed on a host.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index d5c181e8b056..e0a063bd606e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -869,6 +869,20 @@ mmc2: mmc@4022000 {
 			#size-cells = <0>;
 		};
 
+		usb_otg: usb@4100000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-musb",
+				     "allwinner,sun8i-a33-musb";
+			reg = <0x04100000 0x400>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 156 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>;
+			interrupt-names = "mc";
+			clocks = <&ccu CLK_BUS_OTG>;
+			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_OTG>;
+			extcon = <&usbphy 0>;
+			phys = <&usbphy 0>;
+			phy-names = "usb";
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
 		usbphy: phy@4100400 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-usb-phy",
 				     "allwinner,sun20i-d1-usb-phy";
